-- ---------------------------------------------------------------- rewriting
-- under the terminating discipline (lib/match.cub): the oriented rules to the fixpoint, which
-- terminates by the size of the term (here bounded by fuel); the unoriented ones (commutativity
-- shapes) at most n times, the schedule's bound; after each unoriented step the oriented rules run
-- to their fixpoint again. Each step's path is composed onto the path so far (none: refl so far).
-- Tc is the code of the type the path is at (the line of the composition)
-- the path so far p (none: refl) from s, the code the whole path starts at, to m, followed by the
-- step q from m to c', as the code of concat (lib/std.cub):
-- λ i → comp (λ j → T) [ i = 0 ↦ s , i = 1 ↦ q @ j ] (p @ i). Each path is annotated with its
-- type, PathP (λ _ → T) at its endpoints, so its application is inferable (a step is a path
-- abstraction, which checks but does not infer). Under the outer binder i the codes shift by
-- one, under j by two
path-at : Code → Code → Code → Code
path-at Tc a b = cpathp (cplam (code-shift #0 #1 Tc)) a b
